FerrionOS change to the upstream installer (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 16d39fe1f20f15fc97fa3aaa216ac7e449637d41 after the existing recipe patches.

One password: the text and the graphical installer ask for an account name and one password, which becomes that account's login password and the disk passphrase. The installer writes /etc/unlock-slots (mode 0600, root) recording key slot 0 against the account, writes the account name to EFI/BOOT/UNLOCK.TXT for the bootloader's prompt, skips the fast clone, and leaves the password out of the installed filesystem.toml.

